<p>President Trump again threatened strikes on Iran’s bridges and power plants unless Tehran reopened the Strait of Hormuz and accepted a ceasefire-related deal by Tuesday night. Iranian officials rejected the proposal and traded fresh threats with Washington and Israel as fighting stretched into a sixth week. Several reports said the deadline had shifted in recent days, adding uncertainty over whether military escalation or renewed bargaining would follow if no agreement emerged by April 7. At the heart of the dispute is the Strait of Hormuz, a vital shipping lane that carries about a fifth of the world’s oil in peacetime. That gives the crisis global weight far beyond the battlefield. Legal scrutiny also intensified after Trump publicly defended possible attacks on civilian infrastructure. Some experts interviewed by news outlets said those strikes could violate international humanitarian law if they were not justified by military necessity and proportionality rules. On the ground, people in Tehran described growing fear and daily disruption as airstrikes and warning messages fueled concern about broader infrastructure attacks. Even so, some reports pointed to a narrow opening for diplomacy because Trump also said there was still a “good chance” of a deal.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/iGUHJhzNbHzAtKOOByCHQ2TdtlDnYJPudM8690BE4HNEbdwtvVwuZ8sVFuq7amEpZ-XtlbNhMRTRb71Rv2UwSFnl6RDbUOrqojYGy4VLgd753PH33reB5jjqtUd_qSlwHHN009_XqjokErXUwPDNjTjbbe4rfiFQaefcwe2k9tFSehInbek' alt='Damaged buildings in Tehran. President Trump said on Monday that the United States would consider helping to rebuild Iran if they can strike a deal.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Pentagon briefing: Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said U.S. forces were carrying out more strikes on Iran than on any previous day since the war began, underscoring how quickly operations were intensifying as the deadline approached.</li><li>Retaliation threat: PBS said Tehran warned it could launch even more forceful strikes not only on Israel but also on Gulf nations if no ceasefire was reached by Tuesday night.</li><li>Residential area hit: The New York Times live coverage said the Iranian Red Crescent reported that an airstrike hit a residential area of Tehran early Tuesday.</li><li>Proposed terms: A source cited by Reuters in Al-Monitor said a U.S. proposal brokered by Pakistan offered an immediate ceasefire and an end to the effective Hormuz blockade, followed by broader peace talks within 15 to 20 days.</li><li>Negotiating gap: Semafor reported that Iran rejected a U.S.-backed 45-day truce tied to unblocking Hormuz and instead offered counterproposals that Washington dismissed as “maximalist”.</li></ul><blockquote>Tuesday will be Power Plant Day, and Bridge Day, all wrapped up in one - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian military: Iran’s top command called President Trump’s threats “delusional” and said his rhetoric would not weaken Iranian forces. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e49f0110-f07b-4480-9ea4-2b37aab2c906'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>International law experts: Retired Lt. Col. Rachel VanLandingham said attacks on bridges and power plants could be unlawful if they mainly harmed civilians rather than serving a concrete military objective. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/what-international-law-says-about-trumps-threats-to-bomb-irans-bridges-and-power-plants'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Ordinary Iranians: Residents interviewed in Tehran described exhaustion, fear, and practical worries about electricity, transport, and how to protect their families if infrastructure is hit. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvgl0ng8z0do'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump paired military threats with signs that he still believed an agreement was possible and suggested the U.S. might help rebuild Iran after a settlement. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/06/us/politics/trump-iran-cease-fire-proposal.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Pakistan publicly expressed solidarity with the UAE while calling for restraint and de-escalation as the regional crisis intensified. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/06/iran-war-live-updates-trump-hormuz-oil-netanyahu-israel'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-live-hegseth-and-caine-hold-pentagon-briefing-as-trump-threatens-irans-infrastructure'>WATCH LIVE: Hegseth and Caine hold Pentagon briefing as Trump threatens Iran&#x27;s infrastructure</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/35346eaf-0869-4706-8ebb-2d171e15266f'>Trump says US could destroy Iran ‘in one night’ as he demands opening of Hormuz</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/06/world/iran-war-trump-israel'>Trump Renews Threat of Attacks on Iran’s Bridges and Power Plants</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-israel-iran-war-trump-strait-of-hormuz-live-updates-april-6-2026/article70828678.ece'>Iran-Israel war Highlights: Iran army dismisses Trump&#x27;s &#x27;rude, arrogant rhetoric&#x27;</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/7/trumps-threat-to-strike-irans-power-plants-looms'>Trump’s threat to strike Iran’s power plants looms</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-deadline-power-plants-bridges-ceasefire-push-air-force-rescue/'>Trump warns of &quot;critical period&quot; in Iran war as deadline to avoid escalation looms</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-protests-live-blog-trump-khamenei/33640284.html'>Trump Escalates Pressure On Iran With Threat Of Major Military Action</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Military/2026/0406/trump-rescue-iran-bomb-deadline'>If US bombs Iranian infrastructure, could it be a war crime? ‘Not 